<Layout title="Track Record — Apoorva Mehta, MD, MBA">
	<h1>Track Record</h1>
	<p>
		Three separate bets that healthcare needed to be rebuilt, not just
		practiced — each one made before I'd even finished training.
	</p>
	<p>
		I co-founded <strong>ChartR</strong>, an AI-enabled health-tech company,
		to implement operational AI within enterprise healthcare — including
		long-horizon reinforcement learning environments for healthcare and
		clinical AI. It's no longer active, but it's where I learned how hard
		it is to build AI that actually survives contact with a hospital.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before that, as a fellow at <strong>Rock Health Capital</strong>, I
		evaluated hundreds of early-stage digital health startups — commercial,
		technical, and clinical diligence — with end-to-end involvement on
		investments including Vitalize and HealthMC.
	</p>
	<p>
		And earlier, at <strong>SkinCheck</strong>, I helped grow a digital
		dermatology platform to 100,000+ downloads and 6,500 monthly active
		users, shaped its health-plan partnership strategy, and helped raise
		its pre-seed round.
	</p>
</Layout>
